+# #2073 implementation execution record
+
+Implementation base: `69b5b18b377d7fe886390b4d98d2fa0d6d41e85f`. The owner authorized native Plan approval and delivery through Review on 2026-10-20T13:26:11.450Z. Work remains in the recorded bc8d worktree on codex/2039-draft. Previous #2039 child refinement remains paused.
+
+## Approval prerequisites
+
+Fresh native Explain reported the planned-estimate and deep-dive prerequisites. Native plan-approve refused with exit 13 and forecast-missing; it did not grant approval. Code inspection confirmed the configured native adaptive runtime enumerates completed project issues even with no selected comparable IDs. Before running that command, the owner explicitly authorized those historical reads for #2073 only at 2026-10-20T13:30:35.507Z. Original local estimate evidence is unchanged. The retained native input records reviewed WBS hours and logical module areas; native calibrated costs are a distinct forecast.
+
+All native commands retain AITM_GRAPHQL_USAGE=1. Other live reads enroll prepareUsageEnv explicitly. A local checkpoint through 13:37:09.588Z observed 105 calls, 147 known points, 21 unknown costs and zero transport failures since the implementation request. This is partial, includes current workflow reads, and is not an exact HTTP request count. Corpus and done-record observations each reported one point per observation at this checkpoint; do not replace measured costs with a query-complexity guess.
+
+## Clean source baseline
+
+Before any production edit, npm test passed all 974 fast-lane files. Retained local output: .scratch/2073/baseline-fast.log. The runner reported 935 pure-unit and 39 direct-subprocess files; aggregate 115.2 seconds. This is code-baseline evidence, not the paired retained-source traffic benchmark.
+
+## Guard-form observations
+
+A combined document/directory/scratch write was refused before execution because draft writes require explicit Markdown targets. Separate exact-path document writes succeeded. A test command with stderr descriptor redirection was classified as WRITE_CODE in Plan and refused before running; the ordinary supported stdout-log form ran the baseline successfully. No hook, policy or lifecycle state was changed to permit either action. No production file was touched during these prerequisites.
+
+Native plan-estimate converged with forecast record 01M5CRHF99AKZRD6E33GD7P5KW. The prior forecast-missing approval attempt was not counted as approval. Deep-dive posting, canonical mirror and completion checkpoint precede a fresh native approval. Official schema reference inspected without live GraphQL dispatch: [GitHub Projects GraphQL schema](https://docs.github.com/en/graphql/reference/projects).
+
+## Native approval
+
+Native plan-approve succeeded at 2026-10-20T13:54:21Z with human provenance, freezing forecast 01M5CRHF99AKZRD6E33GD7P5KW. The calibrated board/body projection is 9 hours and Size L, distinct from the retained local 6.5-hour estimate. Fresh Explain then reported promote ready with no blockers. Governed one-step promotion was invoked; its completion is pending.
+
+## Admission verification
+
+After conditional admission changes, the fast lane ran all 974 files and reported two bookkeeping failures: package-boundary expected 944 packed entries but the intentional classifier makes 945; GraphQL inventory expected the previous collector call-site line 72 instead of 74. The exact one-module package allowance and relocated call-site expectation were updated. Both affected files then passed all 15 tests. The full fast lane must run again after the remaining implementation; this checkpoint does not claim a green final suite. Layout, story-tag and hard line-cap audits passed.
+
+## Target-reader checkpoint
+
+The new reader API first failed its required-API assertion; project/body validation then passed 27 focused cases, expanded with bounded pagination and legacy-prefix checks. The actual writer integration first failed because it emitted zero TargetBinding calls. After wiring the three concrete adapters, real changed publication completed in 179 dispatches. The retained baseline is 313; outcome equality remains mandatory in the final paired verifier. Old broad authorization/ownership collectors and publication protocol modules remain unchanged.
+
+The compatibility fixture now provides current typed target responses from fresh raw board/body state. One legacy tether test config needed explicit canonical Estimate/Size IDs; production refuses absent definitions instead of substituting a fake null. Shared-writer/recovery tests passed 134/134, and the real public route plus pre-change manifest recovery passed six integrated checks. The bounded route deliberately throws at promotion after completed publication and runs native rollback; it does not claim whole-refine success or savings.
+
+GraphQL capture checkpoint: 591 native workflow observations, 657 known returned points, 165 unknown costs and one non-success observation from implementation authorization through 13:56:40.049Z. Full records are retained in graphql-usage-checkpoint.md. This capture does not expose live response bytes; offline response bytes are reported separately.
+
+## Integrated verification checkpoint
+
+The declared story verifier passed 69 tests, including paired retained/optimized source, fixed-budget failure oracles, actual native source/activity executables, real Plan-exit collection, scalar validation and pre-change recovery. The native executable ledger reports are retained as native-activity-guard-leaf/drift.md and native-source-edit-gate-leaf/drift.md. Native allow is silent exit-zero; each test also requires the expected nonempty successful selected-response ledger.
+
+The complete npm run quality command succeeded: formatting, all repository lint/audit gates and all 975 fast-lane files (123.1 seconds aggregate). Earlier redirected quality/format command forms were refused by the activity classifier before execution; ordinary unredirected npm run quality was supported. The earlier assumption that the alias itself was unsupported was corrected by this successful run.
+
+Spell checking surfaced pre-existing technical terminology and opaque IDs in retained #2039/#2073 documents. Valid project terminology was added to the project dictionary. Exact ID patterns are scoped to the old probe/traffic files, the actual native forecast ID is explicitly ignored, and the immutable historical spelling in plan.r0 plus its configuration entry is scoped to those exact files. Prior accepted artifacts were not rewritten. Full spell checking then passed with zero issues.
+
+Implementation review and exact-head native Test/Review are still pending at this checkpoint. No Review completion or live savings is claimed here.
